Root cause:
The bug was caused by using `ARRAY_SIZE()` to determine the size of a string literal, which led to a compiler warning about a comparison that is always false due to the limited range of the data type. This approach was impractical as it did not accurately reflect the actual length of the string, especially considering the potential inclusion of a null terminator (`\0`), which is not relevant in this context. The correct approach is to use `strlen()` to get the actual length of the string, ensuring proper functionality without compiler warnings.

