BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(sysrq_toggle_seq) >= U8_MAX);
```
Reason:
The use of `ARRAY_SIZE(sysrq_toggle_seq)` to determine the size of a string literal is incorrect, as it does not accurately reflect the actual length of the string. This leads to a compiler warning about a comparison that is always false due to the limited range of the data type, particularly when the string length is less than or equal to 1. The inclusion of the null terminator (`\0`) in the size calculation is impractical in this context.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
int sysrq_toggle_seq_len = strlen(sysrq_toggle_seq);
```
